cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite this release using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Switched-Current Impedance Spectroscopy for PEM Water Electrolysis"
authors:
  - family-names: "Finn"
    given-names: "Hamish"
    affiliation: "School of Engineering, University of Tasmania, Australia"
version: "1.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MATLAB/Simulink simulation of switched-resistor current excitation and
  fundamental impedance reconstruction for a simplified PEM water
  electrolysis equivalent circuit. The workflow evaluates five operating
  points spanning 0.25 to 20 A, with 47 frequencies per point from 10 kHz
  to 1 Hz, and exports figures, error tables and compact result caches.
  Shared current-interrupt functionality is proposed but not validated.
keywords:
  - "electrochemical impedance spectroscopy"
  - "PEM water electrolysis"
  - "switched current"
  - "resistor bank"
  - "MATLAB"
  - "Simulink"
